## 25.3.4.6 Concept input\_or\_output\_iterator

**[iterator.concept.iterator]**

1 The input\_or\_output\_iterator concept forms the basis of the iterator concept taxonomy; every iterator models input\_or\_output\_iterator. This concept specifies operations for dereferencing and incrementing an iterator. Most algorithms will require additional operations to compare iterators with sentinels (25.3.4.7), to read (25.3.4.9) or write (25.3.4.10) values, or to provide a richer set of iterator movements (25.3.4.11, 25.3.4.12, 25.3.4.13).

```txt
template<class I>
  concept input_or_output_iterator =
    requires(I i) {
      { *i } -> can-reference;
      } &&
      weakly_incrementable<I>;

```

