## 26.7.28 Chunk view [range.chunk] 26.7.28.1 Overview [range.chunk.overview]

1 chunk\_view takes a view and a number N and produces a range of views that are N-sized non-overlapping successive chunks of the elements of the original view, in order. The last view in the range can have fewer than N elements.

2 The name views::chunk denotes a range adaptor object (26.7.2). Given subexpressions E and N, the expression views::chunk(E, N) is expression-equivalent to chunk\_view(E, N).

