## 28.5.4.4 Class template subtract\_with\_carry\_engine

**[rand.eng.sub]**

1 A subtract\_with\_carry\_engine random number engine produces unsigned integer random numbers.

2 The state $x_{i}$ of a subtract\_with\_carry\_engine object x is of size $\mathcal{O}(r)$ , and consists of a sequence X of r integer values $0 \leq X_{i} < m = 2^{w}$ ; all subscripts applied to X are to be taken modulo r. The state $x_{i}$ additionally consists of an integer c (known as the carry) whose value is either 0 or 1.

3 The state transition is performed as follows:

<!-- page: 1428 -->

<div class="docvortex-algorithm" style="white-space: pre-wrap; font-family:monospace;">
— Let $Y = X_{i-s} - X_{i-r} - c$.
— Set $X_i$ to $y = Y \mod m$. Set $c$ to 1 if $Y &lt; 0$, otherwise set $c$ to 0.
[Note 1: This algorithm corresponds to a modular linear function of the form $TA(x_i) = (a \cdot x_i) \mod b$, where $b$ is of the form $m^r - m^s + 1$ and $a = b - (b - 1)/m$. — end note]
The generation algorithm is given by $GA(x_i) = y$, where $y$ is the value produced as a result of advancing the engine's state as described above.
