Effects: If \*this does not have ownership of a stop state, returns false. Otherwise, atomically determines whether the owned stop state has received a stop request, and if not, makes a stop request. The determination and making of the stop request are an atomic read-modify-write operation (6.9.2.2). If the request was made, the callbacks registered by associated stop\_callback objects are synchronously called. If an invocation of a callback exits via an exception then terminate is invoked (14.6.2).

