  where no value is returned should explicitly state this as ``return
  None``, and an explicit return statement should be present at the
  end of the function (if reachable):

  .. code-block::
     :class: good

     # Correct:

     def foo(x):
         if x >= 0:
             return math.sqrt(x)
         else:
             return None

     def bar(x):
         if x < 0:
             return None
         return math.sqrt(x)

  .. code-block::
     :class: bad

     # Wrong:

     def foo(x):
         if x >= 0:
             return math.sqrt(x)

     def bar(x):
         if x < 0:
             return
         return math.sqrt(x)

